    "provenance": {
        "origin": "New synthetic byte builders and direct function tests; existing fixtures and expectations unchanged",
        "crcVector": "ASCII 123456789 -> CRC32 cbf43926; empty input -> 0. No CRC implementation copied.",
        "deflateVector": "RFC 1951 final stored block: 01 09 00 f6 ff followed by ASCII 123456789. No compressor/decoder implementation added.",
        "wire": "Frozen PR10 ZXE2/ZXR2/ZIP2 layouts and original PR28 contract",
        "dependencies": "Only existing crate dependencies, no added dev-dependencies"
    },
    "limits": [
        "79 named Rust test functions: three new oracle/overlap cases, stronger per-item success and single-item CRC/malformed failure assertions. Loop mutations remain subcases.",
        "78 assertion tests and one policy observation. Deflate packed-tail acceptance/rejection is printed with --nocapture and is not evidence of C# policy compatibility.",
        "Reviewed production fixes include Unix type precedence, bounded duration parsing, borrowed nested-error classification and metadata failure latching. Execution remains pending.",
        "Allocator activity is not instrumented. Oversized JSON/Source/range requests are checked by no-body-read/no-request observations plus static preallocation review.",
